<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Braniewo</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Braunsberg</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Braniewo, German Braunsberg, is a town in Warmia in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>, near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vistula-lagoon">Vistula Lagoon</a>. Founded in the thirteenth century in the lands of the Prince-Bishopric of Warmia under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a>, it became a member of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanseatic-league">Hanseatic League</a> and a centre of trade. After 1466 it passed with Warmia to Poland, and from 1565 it housed an important <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuit</a> college.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/braniewo.jpg" alt="Braniewo" width="320" height="221" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Archetyp · CC BY-SA 3.0 pl · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Braniewo_-_bazylika_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
